# Copy to .env.local to point the app at a running backend (see ../server/) for local sign-in
# development. Leave unset — the default, including the deployed GitHub Pages build — and the app
# runs exactly as it always has: localStorage-only progress, no account layer at all. Unset, the
# /sign-in and /sign-up routes aren't registered and the "Sign in" link isn't rendered, so nobody
# is offered a form that could only fail on submit; the Progress Dashboard's export/import is the
# backend-free way to move progress between browsers.
#
# Set it and two other things follow: those routes come back, and app/scripts/routes.mjs expects
# them — so export this for the verify run too, not just the build, or the suites report them 404.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080
